---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial Policy"
  description="CapitalColumn's editorial policy covering AI-assisted content, source standards, corrections, and financial disclaimer."
>
  <div class="container">
    <article class="static-page">
      <h1>Editorial Policy</h1>

      <section class="static-section">
        <h2>AI-Assisted Content Policy</h2>
        <p>
          CapitalColumn uses artificial intelligence to assist in researching, drafting, and structuring
          financial news articles. Our AI pipeline scans regulatory filings, press releases, exchange
          data, and trusted news sources to produce article drafts.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every article published on CapitalColumn clearly indicates its production status through
          provenance badges:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>AI-Assisted:</strong> The article was generated with AI assistance and may not have been reviewed by a human editor.</li>
          <li><strong>Editor Reviewed:</strong> A human editor has reviewed the article for accuracy, context, and editorial quality.</li>
          <li><strong>Source Verified:</strong> All primary claims in the article have been traced back to and verified against original sources.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We are committed to being transparent about AI usage. We will never publish AI-generated
          content while pretending it was written by a human journalist.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="static-section">
        <h2>Source Standards</h2>
        <p>
          We prioritize primary sources: company filings, regulatory disclosures, official press
          releases, and verified market data. When secondary sources are used, they are clearly
          attributed.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every article includes source cards at the bottom, listing:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Source name and publisher</li>
          <li>Source type (filing, press release, news article, etc.)</li>
          <li>Whether it is a primary source</li>
          <li>A link to the original document or page</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="static-section">
        <h2>Correction Process</h2>
        <p>
          We take accuracy seriously. When an error is identified — whether by our team, our readers,
          or our automated checks — we follow this process:
        </p>
        <ol>
          <li>The article is updated with the correct information.</li>
          <li>A correction notice is added to the article, clearly describing what was changed and why.</li>
          <li>The correction timestamp is displayed on the article.</li>
          <li>The correction is logged in our audit system.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          To report an error or request a correction, please contact us at
          <a href="mailto:corrections@capitalcolumn.in">corrections@capitalcolumn.in</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="static-section">
        <h2>Financial Disclaimer</h2>
        <p>
          CapitalColumn publishes financial news and analysis for informational purposes only. Nothing
          on this website constitutes financial advice, investment advice, trading advice, or any
          other type of advice.
        </p>
        <p>
          You should not make any financial decision based solely on information published on
          CapitalColumn. Always consult a qualified, licensed financial advisor before making
          investment decisions.
        </p>
        <p>
          Past performance of any security, market sector, or financial product is not indicative of
          future results. All investments involve risk, including the potential loss of principal.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="static-section">
        <h2>Conflict of Interest Statement</h2>
        <p>
          CapitalColumn and its team members may hold positions in securities mentioned in articles.
          Any material conflict of interest will be disclosed in the relevant article.
        </p>
        <p>
          Our editorial coverage is not influenced by advertising revenue, corporate partnerships, or
          external pressures. We do not accept payment for favorable coverage.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="static-section">
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For editorial inquiries: <a href="mailto:hello@capitalcolumn.in">hello@capitalcolumn.in</a>
        </p>
        <p>
          For corrections: <a href="mailto:corrections@capitalcolumn.in">corrections@capitalcolumn.in</a>
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .static-page {
    max-width: var(--max-w-content);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: var(--space-8) 0 var(--space-16);
  }
  .static-page h1 {
    font-size: var(--text-4xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-8);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-6);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }
  .static-section {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
  }
  .static-section h2 {
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }
  .static-section p,
  .static-section li {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    line-height: var(--leading-loose);
    color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  }
  .static-section p {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }
  .static-section ul,
  .static-section ol {
    padding-left: var(--space-6);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
  }
  .static-section li {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
  }
  .static-section a {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }
</style>
